  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girl&apos;&apos;s Right to Secondary Education (Tanzania)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Tanzania, girls&apos; enrolment in secondary school is much lower than boys. Girls are also much more likely to drop out of school. And overall, their performance is a lot worse. There are many and varied reasons for this.  Girls face sexual harassment in the school, and walking to and from school. As a result, teenage pregnancies, and HIV are common. This project seeks to remedy this situation in two rural regions of Tanzania. The project will support local communities to construct and equip supervised girls dormitories in thirty secondary schools. They will provide training for school management committees and local government committees tasked with community development. The result will be an increase in enrolment, retention and performance of girls in secondary schools and a far greater commitment from community leaders in girls&apos; education, and their protection from harassment and abuse.</narrative>
  </description>
